cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Rigidity of harmonic functions on the supercritical percolation cluster: Lean formalization"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/Percolation-Rigidity"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "Rigidity of harmonic functions on the
  supercritical percolation cluster" by Ahmed Bou-Rabee, William Cooperman and Paul Dario, in a
  corrected draft of the arXiv v2 source kept in paper/. All 43 numbered results that the paper
  proves are proved in Lean, with no sorry and only the standard axioms; the other five numbered
  results are quoted from the literature. The proved results include the main theorems: on the
  infinite cluster of supercritical bond percolation, Lipschitz harmonic functions and
  integer-valued harmonic functions of linear growth are constant (Theorems 1.1 and 1.2), in two
  dimensions a function with integer Laplacian of finite support that decays faster than |x|^-1 has
  finite support (Theorem 1.3), and the sandpile Markov chain on the largest cluster of a box mixes
  in time of order n^d log n (Theorem 6.5). The theorems of Rigidity.Assembly.Main take twelve
  results of the literature as explicit hypotheses; all twelve are also proved in Lean, so Theorems
  1.1, 1.2, 1.3 and 6.5 and Proposition 3.2 hold with the supercritical regime p_c(d) < p < 1 as
  their only hypothesis (Rigidity.Assembly.Unconditional). Each of the four main theorems has two
  Mathlib-only comparator challenges, one with the literature inputs as hypotheses and one with the
  regime as its only hypothesis.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
